  "description": "This application seeks planning permission for the installation of a commercial kitchen extraction and ventilation system at 794 Fulham Road, SW6 5SL. The \nsite is in active use as a food-serving premises, and the proposed works are essential to meet environmental health, safety, and operational requirements. The canopy of the extraction system will be 1.2m wide.\nKey components for the  installation of a full extraction and ventilation system for the kitchen located in \nthe basement include\n Duct fan \n Carbon filter \n Silencers \n Jet cowl \n Bird beak terminal \n\nThe airflow strategy is designed in the following way\n\nExtraction Path: \n\n Air is extracted from the basement kitchen. \n Ducting runs vertically up to the roof level of the building. \n Includes carbon filtration and silencers for odour and noise control. \n\n• Fresh Air Inlet: \n\n A fresh air intake will be provided at the rear of the ground floor. \n Fresh air will be delivered down to the basement using ducting that follows the same vertical route as the extraction system. \n This ensures proper air circulation and a compliant kitchen environment.",
